content.text:
id: char-alfred-broome
name: alfred-broome
sketch: "The butler: stoic, old-school, formerly a railway machinist. Knows his
  way around springs and clockwork. Long service to the Hales."
identity: {}
provenance: {}

id: char-owen-myers
name: owen-myers
sketch: Local clock repairman and collector acquaintance of Victor. Skilled with
  small mechanisms, sometimes quarrels with Victor over valuations.
identity: {}
provenance: {}

id: char-lucy-hale
name: lucy-hale
sketch: "Victor's niece and heir-presumptive: practical, plainspoken, lives in
  the house. Financial motive if Victor changes his will."
identity: {}
provenance: {}

id: char-evelyn-ross
name: evelyn-ross
sketch: "Rival collector and a guest that evening: charming, ruthless in
  business, interested in acquiring Victor's most prized automaton."
identity: {}
provenance: {}

id: char-james-cole
name: james-cole
sketch: Narrator and private detective in his mid-40s. Methodical, world-weary,
  sceptical; tells the story in first person.
identity: {}
provenance: {}

id: char-victor-hale
name: victor-hale
sketch: "Victim: a sixty-year-old collector of automatons and clocks,
  proprietorial and sharp-tongued. Killed in his locked study."
identity: {}
provenance: {}
